{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal","id":1511087,"title":"What is Malkav's true goal?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-08T15:31:32-07:00","id":1511087,"title":"What is Malkav's true goal?","content":"So, as the title suggests, I'm talking about the Antediluvian himself. I was talking with a friend who often plays as a Malkavian and he asked me this question and to be honest, it's hard to give a good answer. Naturally, we have those generic easy answers like &quot;win the Jyhad&quot;, etc. But while we get a somewhat clearer picture of other Antediluvians like Saulot or Tremere, for instance, for me at least, despite my decades of experience as a Storyteller, it's not easy to come up with such an answer regarding Malkav, we don't see much of his actions in the setting as we see in other cases and while many regard the Antediluvian Ventrue as &quot;dead and gone&quot;, it's not the case with Malkav.<br /> <br /> So, I ask here to you players and Storytellers, what do you think is Malkav's &quot;ultimate end&quot;, what is his purpose or perhaps even more important, especially relating to what I said before, what are his &quot;means&quot;? How does he feel towards his madness, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T16:00:23-07:00","id":1511088,"title":"","content":"I think he may have already succeeded at it long ago. He wanted to achieve true immortality by becoming a psionic being inhabiting all Malkavians everywhere. That way he can only die if every last Malkavian dies, and it is easy enough for a being with his immense level of telepathic ability to prevent that.<br /> <br /> In other words Malkav won, and he won a long time ago. At most, he subtly schemes against the other Antes to keep them from undoing his win by genociding the Malkavian clan. He's only interested in keeping what he has, so his schemes don't amount to much.<br /> <br /> I think that's also true of Ventrue, who I believe has become living Dominate. The reason he has been known to embrace new 4th gens thousands of years after his death is, he has achieved a level of Dominate so great that he can possess any random Ventrue, thicken their blood to 3rd gen for the duration of the possession, and embrace a 4rth gen. Ventrue didn't die eons ago. Ventrue won eons ago, and is now a spirit who mostly relaxes and enjoys his retirement, perhaps just occasionally engaging in a bit of low-level jyhad to prevent the other Antes from undoing his victory by completely genociding the Ventrue clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T16:32:30-07:00","id":1511089,"title":"","content":"In addition to the obvious, I have two theories.<br /> <br /> 1. The web of madness acts as an escape hatch for him, so his own madness, which I imagine is much worse than in other Malkavians, is assuaged once it is shared with others, and so it continues for as long as the clan persists, the more Malkavians exist, the more his madness is mitigated and the less it gets worse, in this scenario he hopes to one day be almost sane.<br /> <br /> 2. He is very angry with Cain for what he did to him and therefore feels a desire for revenge and thanks to his different vision he can see patterns which allows him to know how to manipulate events and obtain the desired result, the Gehenna, where he will get his revenge and the Malkavian clan is his instrument for this, that's why his visions are imprecise so that they only know what is necessary to act as he wants, that's why they have the impulse to play pranks, they are actions that seem random, and most of the time they are, but in fact they are planned and as many of them are jokes in fact nobody sees the pattern. In short, the entire Malkavian clan is a puppet of Malkav without even realizing it, as he doesn't control with orders or charisma, but with impulses that seem natural.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T16:57:32-07:00","id":1511090,"title":"","content":"Everyone knows the Malkavians are not real. They are a collective hallucination produced by Malkav: each Malkavian is one of his personalities, which are actually psychic representations of his neurons, hence why the web of madness: that's his actual brain.<br /> <br /> As for goal, he's still looking for one, hence why the Malkavians contradict each other about it, some think they know it for sure, some are wholly unsure, etc.: the neurons are still at work examining possible goals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16965,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","user":"Hermeticus","date":". 05-08-2023, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T17:20:25-07:00","id":1511092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal?p=1511088#post1511088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think he may have already succeeded at it long ago. He wanted to achieve true immortality by becoming a psionic being inhabiting all Malkavians everywhere. That way he can only die if every last Malkavian dies, and it is easy enough for a being with his immense level of telepathic ability to prevent that.<br /> <br /> In other words Malkav won, and he won a long time ago. At most, he subtly schemes against the other Antes to keep them from undoing his win by genociding the Malkavian clan. He's only interested in keeping what he has, so his schemes don't amount to much.<br /> <br /> I think that's also true of Ventrue, who I believe has become living Dominate. The reason he has been known to embrace new 4th gens thousands of years after his death is, he has achieved a level of Dominate so great that he can possess any random Ventrue, thicken their blood to 3rd gen for the duration of the possession, and embrace a 4rth gen. Ventrue didn't die eons ago. Ventrue won eons ago, and is now a spirit who mostly relaxes and enjoys his retirement, perhaps just occasionally engaging in a bit of low-level jyhad to prevent the other Antes from undoing his victory by completely genociding the Ventrue clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very interesting theory. So, in your vision, both Ventrue and Malkav have completely transcended their physical nature and became concepts, the fabled &quot;thing in itself&quot;.<br /> <br /> As I said, that's a rather interesting idea, one thing that always comes to mind regarding the Antediluvians is that whenever we create a story we need to imagine who truly &quot;succeeded&quot; and &quot;won&quot;, because then we could run into the problem that is &quot;if everyone has succeeded, nobody really succeeded&quot;, but perhaps that's just another paradox. That is just a thought that came to mind regarding them as it's interesting and somewhat easy to see that each one of them had a similar way to succeed, that is, for instance, it's often stated that Lasombra became something like &quot;the Abyss itself&quot; or &quot;one with the Abyss&quot; and with Tzimisce we have since long time ago this bizarre thing that he is in the blood of all who have experienced his blood, in a similar vein to the controversial take on Vicissitude that the original <i>Dirty Hand</i> came up with in the 90s. So, what I mean is that, in a way, they have all basically achieved &quot;transcendence&quot;. It's a very cool concept to work with, even though in most games these things are not that relevant, as rarely ever would a PC deal directly with an Antediluvian, but then that's definitely not relevant to the discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. The web of madness acts as an escape hatch for him, so his own madness, which I imagine is much worse than in other Malkavians, is assuaged once it is shared with others, and so it continues for as long as the clan persists, the more Malkavians exist, the more his madness is mitigated and the less it gets worse, in this scenario he hopes to one day be almost sane. </div> </div> </div>This complements really well with the theory posted by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3598_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3598\" data-vbnamecard=\"3598\">CajunKhan</a> and it's an interesting take regarding his madness and his way to deal with that, because then again there's one wild idea that &quot;if everybody is crazy, then nobody is truly crazy&quot;. A rather fascinating concept to work with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Everyone knows the Malkavians are not real. They are a collective hallucination produced by Malkav: each Malkavian is one of his personality, which is actually one of his neurons, hence why the web of madness: that's his actual brain.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Hahaha you made me laugh out loud here, because I visualized a Malkavian saying that<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T19:06:03-07:00","id":1511096,"title":"","content":"I am aware that, as VtM metaplot and lore advanced, the writers went for a 3rd Generation as god's/concepts and their powers being plot devices.<br /> I still like to think as them as fundamentally being people. Really old and powerful people, but just people. I also really like them to lie in deep, hidden and well protected tombs, from which they exert control over different Kindred, from their Clan or not, through advanced Auspex, Dominate and other Disciplines. As for their goals, the same as most people have: survival, power and experiences. They don't really have a master plan for Gehenna, because they don't really know even if there will ever be one. Maybe they don't even believe in it, or know that's an invention of younger, telologically inclined, Kindred.<br /> As for Malkav, I envision a deeply disturbed, extremely scared and dangerous individual, who is prone to make unexpected movements in the board of the Jyhad trying to throw their rivals off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T19:55:25-07:00","id":1511100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal?p=1511096#post1511096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am aware that, as VtM metaplot and lore advanced, the writers went for a 3rd Generation as god's/concepts and their powers being plot devices.<br /> I still like to think as them as fundamentally being people. Really old and powerful people, but just people. I also really like them to lie in deep, hidden and well protected tombs, from which they exert control over different Kindred, from their Clan or not, through advanced Auspex, Dominate and other Disciplines. As for their goals, the same as most people have: survival, power and experiences. They don't really have a master plan for Gehenna, because they don't really know even if there will ever be one. Maybe they don't even believe in it, or know that's an invention of younger, telologically inclined, Kindred.<br /> As for Malkav, I envision a deeply disturbed, extremely scared and dangerous individual, who is prone to make unexpected movements in the board of the Jyhad trying to throw their rivals off.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least Haqim and Absiliard think so in some Gehenna scenarios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-08T22:11:42-07:00","id":1511105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal?p=1511096#post1511096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am aware that, as VtM metaplot and lore advanced, the writers went for a 3rd Generation as god's/concepts and their powers being plot devices.<br /> I still like to think as them as fundamentally being people. Really old and powerful people, but just people. I also really like them to lie in deep, hidden and well protected tombs, from which they exert control over different Kindred, from their Clan or not, through advanced Auspex, Dominate and other Disciplines. As for their goals, the same as most people have: survival, power and experiences. They don't really have a master plan for Gehenna, because they don't really know even if there will ever be one. Maybe they don't even believe in it, or know that's an invention of younger, telologically inclined, Kindred.<br /> As for Malkav, I envision a deeply disturbed, extremely scared and dangerous individual, who is prone to make unexpected movements in the board of the Jyhad trying to throw their rivals off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Over the course of the years, I've been many times inclined to also prefer to see them as &quot;fundamentally people&quot;, although really strange people with godlike powers, but &quot;people&quot; in that sense you meant it. I remember my first &quot;shock&quot; came when I read they made Saulot into a master schemer who planned Tremere's diablerie on him in order to just manipulate/use him to advance his plans, I think this whole idea of &quot;3rd generations as being gods and essentially plot devices&quot; kind of started with this change in the metaplot a. Because before that, I thought that, even though they had &quot;godlike&quot; powers, it would be still possible to defeat them, like the first idea of Tremere diablerizing Saulot (and Augustus Giovanni diablerizing Ashur/Capadocius), in a sense that political maneuver and the wheels of time moving could mean an Antediluvian (and in these two cases whole clans) could be defeated/destroyed, etc and become history. But after Transylvania Chronicles and all these changes in the metaplot (which some of my friends hated, I remember). I started to experiment with these ideas of a &quot;master plan&quot; like Saulot's, so this development, specifically Saulot's, which I believe was the first, utterly changed the picture of the game in my opinion.<br /> <br /> So that now it seems, Antediluvian became something entirely different in the metaplot, so the visions shared here reflect this, like Malkav becoming an &quot;idea/concept&quot;, Tzimisce being &quot;everywhere&quot;, Lasombra &quot;being the Abyss&quot;, etc. I think it all started with Saulot's actions that utterly changed the game, for good or bad, depending on the point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T02:34:30-07:00","id":1511114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal?p=1511105#post1511105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Over the course of the years, I've been many times inclined to also prefer to see them as &quot;fundamentally people&quot;, although really strange people with godlike powers, but &quot;people&quot; in that sense you meant it. I remember my first &quot;shock&quot; came when I read they made Saulot into a master schemer who planned Tremere's diablerie on him in order to just manipulate/use him to advance his plans, I think this whole idea of &quot;3rd generations as being gods and essentially plot devices&quot; kind of started with this change in the metaplot a. Because before that, I thought that, even though they had &quot;godlike&quot; powers, it would be still possible to defeat them, like the first idea of Tremere diablerizing Saulot (and Augustus Giovanni diablerizing Ashur/Capadocius), in a sense that political maneuver and the wheels of time moving could mean an Antediluvian (and in these two cases whole clans) could be defeated/destroyed, etc and become history. But after Transylvania Chronicles and all these changes in the metaplot (which some of my friends hated, I remember). I started to experiment with these ideas of a &quot;master plan&quot; like Saulot's, so this development, specifically Saulot's, which I believe was the first, utterly changed the picture of the game in my opinion.<br /> <br /> So that now it seems, Antediluvian became something entirely different in the metaplot, so the visions shared here reflect this, like Malkav becoming an &quot;idea/concept&quot;, Tzimisce being &quot;everywhere&quot;, Lasombra &quot;being the Abyss&quot;, etc. I think it all started with Saulot's actions that utterly changed the game, for good or bad, depending on the point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>It definitely started with Saulot, when some writers decided he was too cool and decided to bring him back with that, IMO, absurd plot. I, like those friends you mentioned, absolutely hated those changes. In the games I ST, Saulot is dead because he arrived to the conclusion giving up the Jyhad was his only way to the redemption he desperately sought, and that's a great story ending for him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T11:41:56-07:00","id":1511146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal?p=1511114#post1511114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It definitely started with Saulot, when some writers decided he was too cool and decided to bring him back with that, IMO, absurd plot. I, like those friends you mentioned, absolutely hated those changes. In the games I ST, Saulot is dead because he arrived to the conclusion giving up the Jyhad was his only way to the redemption he desperately sought, and that's a great story ending for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting take on Saulot, for sure. In many stories I ST in the past he was really destroyed and diablerized by Tremere, what I think is also a great way to explain the success of the clan as whole, despite fighting on many fronts. I believe to completely adopt the idea of absorbing all (or most) powers of the Cainite (something that was always implied in any case by the way, just implemented differently in some editions in order to players not benefit too much from diablerie, to be sincere) you diablerize makes it much easier to explain the changes that occurred in the setting over the last 1000 years or so. Otherwise, with gods as Antediluvians and demigods as the Methusaleh who know everything in advance and everything is part of their plan it's very hard to satisfactorily explain these things without making them looking a little silly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 05-09-2023, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T13:13:02-07:00","id":1511149,"title":"","content":"I find it hard to determine what exactly each Antedeluvian wants in the Jyhad. It's not clear Gehenna is a Highlander type situation where there can be only one. While some Antedeluvians may want to kill all the others, some may not (they may only want to destroy some, or none at all as long as they are allowed to live.) Some Antdeluvians might even be allies with one another. And until I 1) figure out how I think Gehenna might play out or even would actually look like and 2) determine how this would be relevant in how I actually run the game, I'll probably never bother to answer these kind of questions as an ST.<br /> <br /> Though I do think it's fine for players to speculate these things because these are fun kind of questions to wonder about. It's just they are not actually relevant in game.<br /> <br /> I do agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27429\" data-vbnamecard=\"27429\">Microcuchon</a> that I still want them to be actual persons. I don't agree with the idea that they can somehow depersonalize and &quot;become&quot; this immaterial thing or that. Even bizarre things like Cappadocious going full occult bonkers in an attempt to become God in some bizarre Gnostic ritual can be understood in that way.<br /> <br /> In terms of explaining the Malkavian Madness Network, I do not hold that it &quot;is&quot; Malkav. Instead, my interpretation is that its existence is because of a unique Level 10 Discipline (likely Auspex) of Malkav's. Without Malkav learning that Discipline, the network wouldn't exist. (Which means for some length of historical time, Malkavians wouldn't have it.) And if Malkav was ever truly destroyed, the Network would cease to exist.<br /> <br /> I don't think Antedeluvians necessarily know any level 10 Disciplines. They simply have the potential to do so because of their Generation. Indeed, I would probably rule in my chronicles that most Antedeluvians do not know level 10 Disciplines (certainly none of the third generation who diablerized to that status know any level 10). But in terms of justifying anomalous things like the Madness Network, I think it's a good justification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T14:32:43-07:00","id":1511157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though I do think it's fine for players to speculate these things because these are fun kind of questions to wonder about. It's just they are not actually relevant in game. </div> </div> </div>As a ST, these things are sometimes necessary in order to make a long term story, I've never been a fan of &quot;one shot&quot; stories, usually my chronicles last for years in real life (and centuries in game), so it's often important for me to know what the highest levels of machinations are really happening in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if Malkav was ever truly destroyed, the Network would cease to exist.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>I particularly like the idea of it &quot;surviving his destruction&quot;, like an echo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think Antedeluvians necessarily know any level 10 Disciplines. They simply have the potential to do so because of their Generation. Indeed, I would probably rule in my chronicles that most Antedeluvians do not know level 10 Disciplines (certainly none of the third generation who diablerized to that status know any level 10). But in terms of justifying anomalous things like the Madness Network, I think it's a good justification. </div> </div> </div>At least canonically they all have at the very least their &quot;theme&quot; disciplines at level 10 and some others that are not defined and are up to the ST to decide and I really agree with that stance, otherwise, at the end of the day it wouldn't make much sense for level 10 disciplines existing at all. Regarding the ones who diablerized to become Antediluvians, I don't see their powers being any less than the others(in the Gehenna scenarios, for instance, the only Antediluvian who is often stated as being weaker is Augustus, and not because of his age, but rather because he couldn't even &quot;complete&quot; his diablerie, Tremere, on the other hand, IIRC was able to beat other Antediluvians namely his nemesis Tzimisce, in two scenarios if I'm not mistaken), as I stated, the best way to make things in the setting make sense is the idea of a Cainite absorbing all the powers of the diablerized through the act of diablerie, and it has always been somewhat implied that it's what in fact happens on a narrative level. This way, I really love the rules provided in the <i>V20 </i>Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra that finally addressed the issue with not so many &quot;if the ST wants, the diablerist could gain some permanent powers&quot;, etc. I find it the only reasonable explanation for Cainites acquiring a huge amount of power in a short time span (we have cases of Cainites that acquired level 9 and 8 in a few disciplines in a little more than 1 century). Otherwise, a great deal of the setting falls apart. The rules presented in <i>The Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra</i> made me rejoice for finally addressing this situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 05-10-2023, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T14:49:49-07:00","id":1511158,"title":"","content":"Back to topic, I wonder how would Malkav's relationship with his brothers be. There are some legends that Saulot was his friend, etc. But little regarding the others. Caine is a distant figure in my opinion. Since I started Storytelling A LONG TIME AGO, I've never ever actually used him. I prefer to see him as someone &quot;who isn't there anymore&quot; or &quot;just doesn't care&quot; about the rest of the cainites, I don't know why, but I've never liked the idea of using him in a story, one of the reasons I found Berlin by Night &quot;too wild&quot; for my tastes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T01:00:23-07:00","id":1511197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal?p=1511157#post1511157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a ST, these things are sometimes necessary in order to make a long term story, I've never been a fan of &quot;one shot&quot; stories, usually my chronicles last for years in real life (and centuries in game), so it's often important for me to know what the highest levels of machinations are really happening in the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I particularly like the idea of it &quot;surviving his destruction&quot;, like an echo.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> At least canonically they all have at the very least their &quot;theme&quot; disciplines at level 10 and some others that are not defined and are up to the ST to decide and I really agree with that stance, otherwise, at the end of the day it wouldn't make much sense for level 10 disciplines existing at all. Regarding the ones who diablerized to become Antediluvians, I don't see their powers being any less than the others(in the Gehenna scenarios, for instance, the only Antediluvian who is often stated as being weaker is Augustus, and not because of his age, but rather because he couldn't even &quot;complete&quot; his diablerie, Tremere, on the other hand, IIRC was able to beat other Antediluviansnamly his nemesis Tzimisce, in two scenarios if I'm not mistaken), as I stated, the best way to make things in the setting make sense is the idea of a Cainite absorbing all the powers of the diablerized through the act of diablerie, and it has always been somewhat implied that it's what in fact happens on a narrative level. This way, I really love the rules provided in the <i>V20 </i>Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra that finally addressed the issue with not so many &quot;if the ST wants, the diablerist could gain some permanent powers&quot;, etc. I find it the only reasonable explanation for Cainites acquiring a huge amount of power in a short time span (we have cases of Cainites that acquired level 9 and 8 in a few disciplines in a little more than 1 century). Otherwise, a great deal of the setting falls apart. The rules presented in <i>The Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra</i> made me rejoice for finally addressing this situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also like to plan ahead and have a general idea of the &quot;big game&quot; even if only affects my game tangentially. I am currently considering ST'ing a ages spanning game chronicle so this issue will become more important if I go for It.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T12:30:38-07:00","id":1511255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal?p=1511197#post1511197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also like to plan ahead and have a general idea of the &quot;big game&quot; even if only affects my game tangentially. I am currently considering ST'ing a ages spanning game chronicle so this issue will become more important if I go for It.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it's a very nice idea to play around and the sensation you get when the players start to discuss things that happened in the course of the game and were related to a particular plot centuries old is wonderful. I love to see my players discussing the things that happen in game, trying to find an explanation and who is behind it all, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T09:47:16-07:00","id":1511547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal#post1511087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, as the title suggests, I'm talking about the Antediluvian himself. I was talking with a friend who often plays as a Malkavian and he asked me this question and to be honest, it's hard to give a good answer. Naturally, we have those generic easy answers like &quot;win the Jyhad&quot;, etc. But while we get a somewhat clearer picture of other Antediluvians like Saulot or Tremere, for instance, for me at least, despite my decades of experience as a Storyteller, it's not easy to come up with such an answer regarding Malkav, we don't see much of his actions in the setting as we see in other cases and while many regard the Antediluvian Ventrue as &quot;dead and gone&quot;, it's not the case with Malkav.<br /> <br /> So, I ask here to you players and Storytellers, what do you think is Malkav's &quot;ultimate end&quot;, what is his purpose or perhaps even more important, especially relating to what I said before, what are his &quot;means&quot;? How does he feel towards his madness, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going with wanting to survive the Jyhad and followed a similar path of Gangrel, Ventrue, Lasombra and Tzismce to move beyond having a single form and maybe getting back at Cain for being a bastard. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T11:23:27-07:00","id":1511555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal?p=1511547#post1511547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going with wanting to survive the Jyhad and followed a similar path of Gangrel, Ventrue, Lasombra and Tzismce to move beyond having a single form and maybe getting back at Cain for being a bastard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Poor Cain, always misunderstood, hahaha. Regarding Malkav again, I've reread <b>Fountains of Bright Crimson</b> (I've read it for the first time some years ago, so I wanted to remember if there was any mention of his actions and purposes there...)last week, and he's basically &quot;just chillin&quot; under Jerusalem for some reason, he's a rather enigmatic Antediluvian, I gotta say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T11:26:03-07:00","id":1511556,"title":"","content":"<br /> I would like to think Malkav wants to understand Caine, and is either waiting for Gehenna, or buying time to postpone it until something is achieved (maybe finding Caine's motivations).<br /> In a way, in my mind, Malkav is like Odin, trying to stop the inevitable (Ragnarok), in this case Gehenna. Like, if Gehenna happens every 10 generations or so, or whatever, in a cyclical way, Malkav would probably want to stop it at some point. The point of a prophet is to guide the way to Heaven or stop the coming of a Disaster, so that would probably be where the Antediluvian of foresight and unknowable plots would be doing.<br /> Basis for my ideas on this is the anecdote, from Libelus Sanguinis if I'm not mistaken, about Malkav and Caine. <br /> <img title=\"Mist\u00e9rio de Malkav parte2.jpg\" data-tempid=\"temp_1237_1684002107006_2\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1237\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1237\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1237&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"Mist\u00e9rio de Malkav parte2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T21:39:02-07:00","id":1511581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal?p=1511556#post1511556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to think Malkav wants to understand Caine, and is either waiting for Gehenna, or buying time to postpone it until something is achieved (maybe finding Caine's motivations).<br /> In a way, in my mind, Malkav is like Odin, trying to stop the inevitable (Ragnarok), in this case Gehenna. Like, if Gehenna happens every 10 generations or so, or whatever, in a cyclical way, Malkav would probably want to stop it at some point. The point of a prophet is to guide the way to Heaven or stop the coming of a Disaster, so that would probably be where the Antediluvian of foresight and unknowable plots would be doing.<br /> Basis for my ideas on this is the anecdote, from Libelus Sanguinis if I'm not mistaken, about Malkav and Caine.<br /> <img title=\"Mist\u00e9rio de Malkav parte2.jpg\" data-tempid=\"temp_1237_1684002107006_2\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1237\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1237\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1237&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"Mist\u00e9rio de Malkav parte2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Very interesting connection you made there. I've never thought about it this way, I mean to see this connection between Malkav and Odin in this way. As a prophet trying to stop the inevitable, it's a good analogy, all in all (and I love Norse Mythology, so I'm a bit biased lol, even though I guess you said that metaphorically) I'll look for the anecdote you mention is in <i>Libelus Sanguinis</i>. One thing that makes me wonder is that while he's said to have been torn apart, he was under Jerusalem, so I guess the Storyteller needs to choose which version he prefers, because according to Fountains of Bright Crimson, he is definitely there under Jerusalem. On the other hand, the Black Hand (&quot;perhaps&quot; no pun intended lol)says the being under Jerusalem is actually Malakai (his Twin Sister), an even more enigmatic Antediluvian.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-13T23:08:09-07:00","id":1511584,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, Malkav is not a nice chap trying to stop Gehenna, but one of the most devious players of the Jyhad. His strategy is to sow mistrust and paranoia among his rivals, using &quot;prophecy&quot; he basically invents and sends through the Malkavian network, to mislead and cause chaos. This way he gets his rivals to fight each other while his own pieces are spared for their prophetic value.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T10:25:21-07:00","id":1511625,"title":"","content":"Very duplicitous and subtle of Malkav. I can totally see it as a possibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T15:56:48-07:00","id":1511666,"title":"","content":"<img title=\"Malkav&#39;s Mystery\" width=\"564\" height=\"798\" data-align=\"none\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/564x/e3/a4/3a/e3a43ab6d46e9b1a6ba993aaac90420a.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.pinimg.com/564x/e3/a4/3a/e3a43ab6d46e9b1a6ba993aaac90420a.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.pinimg.com/564x/e3/a4/3a/e3a43ab6d46e9b1a6ba993aaac90420a.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"Malkav&#39;s Mystery\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> Malkav's Mystery<br /> <br /> I'm not saying Malkav is a nice dude or gal trying to do niceties. But I also don't see Malkav as a malicious individual, but misunderstood. To me, they are way more curious and in search of some truth or understanding, rather than just making the other Antes getting dunked. If the other Antes are to be dunked, than it is to impede them from destroying everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":25534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","user":"Banu_Saulot","date":". 05-14-2023, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T17:11:44-07:00","id":1511676,"title":"","content":"I guess I could choose the final death if I was him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T17:31:14-07:00","id":1511679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal?p=1511666#post1511666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img title=\"Malkav&#39;s Mystery\" width=\"564\" height=\"798\" data-align=\"none\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/564x/e3/a4/3a/e3a43ab6d46e9b1a6ba993aaac90420a.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.pinimg.com/564x/e3/a4/3a/e3a43ab6d46e9b1a6ba993aaac90420a.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.pinimg.com/564x/e3/a4/3a/e3a43ab6d46e9b1a6ba993aaac90420a.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"Malkav&#39;s Mystery\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> Malkav's Mystery<br /> <br /> I'm not saying Malkav is a nice dude or gal trying to do niceties. But I also don't see Malkav as a malicious individual, but misunderstood. To me, they are way more curious and in search of some truth or understanding, rather than just making the other Antes getting dunked. If the other Antes are to be dunked, than it is to impede them from destroying everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or... What's in that text could just be propaganda to make people think he's harmless","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T10:49:43-07:00","id":1511813,"title":"","content":"Of course it could be propaganda. Just as the entire Book of Nod is.<br /> Therein lies the problem, if you consider everything faux, than nothing is true. So there would be no point in basing anything in the views of the books, for there is close to none first contacts. Save Cappadocius, Malkav's somewhat influence in Jerusalem, and the Eldest (in the Dark Age books and Transylvania Chronicles). And even then, it's pretty sketchy, on purpose. <br /> <br /> But there is this thing.... Excluding Saulot, I don't remember no other Antediluvian giving much interest to being seen as a 'nice vamp'. Why should they care, their pawns and rooks will not be any less useful if they hated their Antes guts, perhaps much the contrary. <br /> <br /> Although harmless is a stretch. I doubt any Ante could be considered as such. Unknowable yes. Harmless no. And no piece of lore will really propose that, not without serious contestance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T15:38:59-07:00","id":1511829,"title":"","content":"At this point the Antidiluvians don't care about how you feel about them at this point as there days as living breathing humans are long behind them and you are tools to be used in there plots against each other. It would like the Emporeror In Warhammer 40K as he doesn't have much paternal feelings towards his Primarch children and sees them as useful tools in his plans to strengthen and protect humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T19:51:56-07:00","id":1511841,"title":"","content":"Of course the Antes mind how you feel about them. The Jyhad is a war, and propaganda has been a tool of war since, well, forever. You can't be using Dominate with everyone all the time. It's easier if you send them a vision and they follow it because they think you are the good guy in a good quest for everyone's benefit.<br /> The book of Nod and sources are still useful for the ST because they help us understand how the Antes are perceived and what whoever wrote them wants other people to think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T15:34:41-07:00","id":1511927,"title":"","content":"I would go with something more subtle by sending plots throughout there line and make them think it was there own plans and such people think they are fighting them, but in reality they are helping them. But I still think at this point most of the 3rd generation wouldn't really care how they regarded anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T19:33:45-07:00","id":1511956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal?p=1511927#post1511927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would go with something more subtle by sending plots throughout there line and make them think it was there own plans and such people think they are fighting them, but in reality they are helping them. But I still think at this point most of the 3rd generation wouldn't really care how they regarded anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Care, as in a emotional level, probably not. Mind, as in a strategical level, most likely yes, because it's convenient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T21:16:00-07:00","id":1511968,"title":"","content":"Of all the Antediluvians, I imagine Malkav's goals are probably going to be the hardest to figure out. In my games his goals, whatever they are, don't have much of anything to do with the mortal world. If Malkav won the Jyhad, nobody would know, the world wouldn't change in any sort of noticeable way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T12:17:04-07:00","id":1512034,"title":"","content":"Now that I've read others' posts and given some thought, I have some ideas. First, the Malkavian theme overall is an attempt to understand reality. And that Book of Nod excerpt has his asking &quot;Why&quot; which is a basic philosophical question. So in terms of what Malkav is actually doing is trying to understand existence. He's a philosopher, and probably most concerned about metaphysics and eschatology. Once he moves on to asking Caine &quot;Why?&quot;, the next natural steps would be to ask God &quot;Why?&quot; <br /> <br /> In regards to Gehenna, which should be an end of the world scenario (I heavily dislike the idea that Gehenna can happen multiple times or that the game as we know it can continue afterwards), Malkav is probably most concerned with its actual purpose in the grand scheme of things. Why is this happening? What is the divine plan? What is Caine's role in it? What is my own and those of the other Antedeluvians? What is going to come afterwards?<br /> <br /> Only once he understands the purpose of such things, would Malkav really attempt to do anything. Because he doesn't know what he should do until then. And by the time Gehenna starts, Malkav probably still won't know. So best to do nothing until he does know. He hopes that before the actual End of the World comes, he will figure it out. Maybe he even has decided that he has a role to play, and therefore it is critical he must survive until the end so he can do whatever it is that he needs to do.<br /> <br /> Now this seems to make him a very passive Antedeluvian then at first glance. He has no master plan. He is not trying to build an empire. Or change the nature of reality through occult practice. Or destroy the other Antedeluvians. And so on.<br /> <br /> But I do think we can have Malkav do things. He observes. He studies. And he likely conducts &quot;experiments&quot;. That leads to some practical ideas.<br /> <br /> First, it can explain why he is so protective of his own clan and produces things like the Malkavian Madness Network to give them an edge in survival. They are one of the primary means by which he conducts experiments (at some point, some of them are going to do something interesting). <br /> <br /> Second, he might intervene in some specific ways to preserve the existence of particular vampires (of his own clan or even of others) for the same purpose. He wants to see what happens if they survive or are successful. This does not always mean he only preserves lives of vampires. Sometimes &quot;success&quot; might mean the destruction of vampires. For example, maybe Malkav came to the conclusion that Saulot wanted to be destroyed. He finds that interesting. Why would Saulot want that? Oh, look, there's Tremere (Etrius, Goratrix, whoever) attempting to find an Antedeluvian to diablerize. Hmm, they aren't as smart as they think, and they're never going to find one. If I want to see what will happen by Saulot being destroyed like he wants, I should help them. Lasombra is always destroying his childer. What happens if I do something that encourages that Montano lad to stay loyal and always obey. What will Lasombra do then?<br /> <br /> Third, he will want to collect knowledge. He can't conduct every experiment himself. Other people will do lots of things on their own. He just needs to benefit from what they learn. If he wants to understand what Cappadocious has learned in his study on death, he needs someone who can gain that knowledge for him and bring it into the open. Maybe that explains why Lady Theophana joined the Conspiracy of Isaac - it was a way to bring out Cappadocius's knowledge to the greater population. Or any number of other incidents that seem contrived, incredibly lucky, or inexplicable.<br /> <br /> Fourth, we might use this as some kind of presence behind the Inconnu - who mainly seem to exist in the setting to monitor things.<br /> <br /> Fifth, we could decide any number of mysteries are critically important to Malkav like the nature of Golconda, what the Beast really is, and so on. He really wants to know everything about that, and some of his most important &quot;studies&quot; or &quot;experiments&quot; are based on that.<br /> <br /> Given this, the ST can still decide how Malkav approaches his increasing knowledge. How benevolent or malevolent his approach can suit whatever the ST wants. Not all knowledge is equal, and the older Malkav gets, he probably gets more philosophical and esoteric. So earlier on, there might be more practical approaches along the lines of natural philosophy, and later on it becomes more metaphysical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T13:19:41-07:00","id":1512041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal?p=1511968#post1511968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of all the Antediluvians, I imagine Malkav's goals are probably going to be the hardest to figure out. In my games his goals, whatever they are, don't have much of anything to do with the mortal world. If Malkav won the Jyhad, nobody would know, the world wouldn't change in any sort of noticeable way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or perhaps the people of Earth find themselves beset by strange visions and insights into how perceptions of reality can be altered and find themselves struggling with all these mind expanding ideas as unintentional side effect. Perhaps the Jyhad acts as means as keeping all of them in check in messing with humanity to much. I'm just spit balling here and could be off base with the notion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T15:20:18-07:00","id":1512051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal?p=1512041#post1512041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or perhaps the people of Earth find themselves beset by strange visions and insights into how perceptions of reality can be altered and find themselves struggling with all these mind expanding ideas as unintentional side effect. Perhaps the Jyhad acts as means as keeping all of them in check in messing with humanity to much. I'm just spit balling here and could be off base with the notion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would be funny if the end result of Malkav winning the Jyhad would be to give the world a mushroom acid trip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T18:21:32-07:00","id":1512071,"title":"","content":"It would be a weird way for a member of the 3rd generation to be the last one standing to be remembered as a bringer of a world wide high.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-19-2023, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T18:57:33-07:00","id":1512077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal?p=1511968#post1511968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of all the Antediluvians, I imagine Malkav's goals are probably going to be the hardest to figure out. In my games his goals, whatever they are, don't have much of anything to do with the mortal world. If Malkav won the Jyhad, nobody would know, the world wouldn't change in any sort of noticeable way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree that Malkav doesn't have any intentions regarding the mortal world. He's just interested in his personal obsessions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T09:35:47-07:00","id":1512120,"title":"","content":"Which is why is he preferable over the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T11:35:22-07:00","id":1512127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal?p=1512120#post1512120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is why is he preferable over the others.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that depends on who you are and what are your values. Additionally, I can see Malkav being ok with nuclear warfare if it suits his goals, which doesn't make him that preferable \ud83e\udd37\ud83c\udffb\u200d\u2642\ufe0f","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T09:23:30-07:00","id":1512218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal?p=1512127#post1512127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess that depends on who you are and what are your values. Additionally, I can see Malkav being ok with nuclear warfare if it suits his goals, which doesn't make him that preferable \ud83e\udd37\ud83c\udffb\u200d\u2642\ufe0f</div> </div> </div> </div>True and I never saw him as particularly murderous towards Humanity in general and at best is indifferent and might see them as a source of insight to figure out the visions he is &quot;gifted&quot; with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T18:12:10-07:00","id":1512244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal?p=1512218#post1512218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True and I never saw him as particularly murderous towards Humanity in general and at best is indifferent and might see them as a source of insight to figure out the visions he is &quot;gifted&quot; with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most humans aren't particularly murderous towards ants. That doesn't mean we won't destroy s colony if it happens to be in our way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T21:37:52-07:00","id":1512253,"title":"","content":"As I side note, I don't consider Malkavian &quot;prophetic powers&quot; are actually able to predict the future. In my canon they are either an extremely acute insight in the present situation or a manipulation by external powers. This is done mostly for philosophical reasons, as the idea of true prophecy is antithetical to my own ideas about free will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T09:23:12-07:00","id":1512464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal?p=1512253#post1512253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I side note, I don't consider Malkavian &quot;prophetic powers&quot; are actually able to predict the future. In my canon they are either an extremely acute insight in the present situation or a manipulation by external powers. This is done mostly for philosophical reasons, as the idea of true prophecy is antithetical to my own ideas about free will.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the question is how much free will do Kindred truly have as it's been strongly hinted by Montano and others that you are only allowed so much freedom by your elders &amp; ancients in the war.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T20:58:50-07:00","id":1512539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511087-what-is-malkav-s-true-goal?p=1512464#post1512464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is the question is how much free will do Kindred truly have as it's been strongly hinted by Montano and others that you are only allowed so much freedom by your elders &amp; ancients in the war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Free will conditioned by the Jyhad and the Elders and constrained by prophecy and destiny should not be confused. I am perfectly fine with the first one, and is actually one of the main themes of my chronicles. I dislike the second one, and in my opinion it cheapens the second one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-24T19:30:45-07:00","id":1512668,"title":"","content":"Well, my viewpoint is that Malkav is obsessed with the TRUTH, the final, ultimate why. But at the same time, his very human mind can't grasp it, so he's forever hunting this Grail and unable to understand it. A very frustrated Ante, truly. And as a consequence, his kids can have bizarre insights and visions inside their madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T17:41:23-07:00","id":1512802,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I very much agree with MrDrika.<br /> Antes aren't really caring for a material victory over the Jyhad, or even dominating the world. Not in my opinion and views on the matter, at least.<br /> <br /> They are after truly metaphysical and epic pursuits, of which we won't really understand or grasp. That for me give some sense to the almost schizophrenic stances of Saulot, for there are some many layers and depths, that the writers and storytellers can work to whicever directions suits best. Maybe Saulot wants to become god, maybe a new Christ, maybe he really is humble and wants the best for humanity, in opposition to all vampires, maybe something else entirely. Who knows?<br /> <br /> So when it comes to Malkav, well, anything goes. They might be trying to end vampirism, to end the Jyhad, to find God, to connect every vampire in the world, to make all mortals have True Faith... But to me it's clear it got something to do with knowledge and/or understanding. Be it a very direct information, or a very deep comprehension (and maybe not for Malkav themself, but others).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}